From: Nuxel <nuxel@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH 0027] sensorhub/ssp: complete native BCM47752 firmware download

Implements the FULL kernel-coordinated two-phase BCM47752 boot-ROM firmware
download that the vendor lhd user-space daemon performs, in the kernel before
initialize_mcu()/WHOAMI.  This is the actual missing link identified in
SSP-COLD-BOOT-ROOT-CAUSE.md: the download is a two-phase protocol and both
phases must run over DIRECT bcm_spi_sync()/bcm_ssi_rx() (NOT the hello-gated
/dev/ttyBCM circ-buffer path).

Phase 1 (ROM sync): vendor byte-exact autobaud (32 x 0x80) + raw GetVersion
ping (bcm_gps_regs.c::bcm477x_rpc_get_version transaction_1st/2nd) driven over
direct SPI; polls bcm_ssi_rx() for a real, well-formed GetVersion reply and
does NOT report success on a silent hub (fixes the vendor function's inverted
poll loop and unconditional return 0).

Phase 2 (firmware download): decode the embedded bbd_patch[] container
(<PatchAddress=...> entry point + <Blob=...> hex payload), parse the F0..F5
records, and dispatch each F1 record as a MemoryWrite (RPC id 5, body =
LE32 dest + LE16 count + data) with a per-write reliable ACK requirement, then
StartScratchApp (RPC 46) + ServiceStart (RPC 55) + a verified post-download
GetVersion (RPC 0).  Every stage is evidence-gated; a partial transfer or a
silent hub returns a distinct negative error and never reaches WHOAMI.

